New STM32 project

  STM32 projects need nvim-project.lua plus a Makefile, not openocd.cfg. OpenOCD is set from nvim-project.lua.
  - nvim-project.lua: copy it, then change:
    - openocd_target, for the chip family (target/stm32g4x.cfg, target/stm32f4x.cfg, …). If you leave it out, it defaults to U0, so for any other family you must set it.
    - defaults: the LiveWatch variables. The template's counter, button_presses and the PA5/PC13 bits only make sense on the hello world.
    - halt_commands, if you want a timer frozen (DBGMCU address from the reference manual).
    - serial_baud, if it isn't 115200.
  - Makefile: nvim reads TARGET and BUILD (or CubeMX's BUILD_DIR) from it to find build/<TARGET>.elf. Either a plain STM32CubeMX Makefile
    project, or the template's Makefile (same CubeMX layout): edit TARGET, C_SOURCES, ASM_SOURCES, CPU/FPU/FLOAT-ABI,
    C_DEFS, C_INCLUDES, LDSCRIPT. The template's README explains this.
  - Run <leader>mc once (make clean && bear -- make), so clangd gets compile_commands.json. Redo it after adding files or changing flags.

Debug info: -g vs -g3 (LiveWatch / dap expressions)

  - With -g, gdb knows variables, types, functions: globals/statics (uwTick, counter), struct members, locals.
  - Only -g3 adds the #define macros (GPIOA, TIM1, LED4_PIN, ...). Without it, LiveWatch shows
    'No symbol "GPIOA" in current context' for an expression like GPIOA->ODR.
  - Our template Makefile (CubeMX layout) already has CFLAGS += -g3 in the same ifeq ($(DEBUG), 1) block shown below.
  - A plain STM32CubeMX "Makefile" project has, in the "# compile gcc flags" section:
        ifeq ($(DEBUG), 1)
        CFLAGS += -g -gdwarf-2
        endif
    Change that middle line to:
        CFLAGS += -g3
    then make clean + <leader>mb (or <leader>mB) and flash again. CubeMX has no option for it and rewrites
    the Makefile on every Generate Code, so the change must be redone each time.
  - Alternative that works with plain -g (no Makefile change): use the register struct type plus the base address
    (from the chip header stm32xxxx.h, *_BASE defines, or the reference manual) in nvim-project.lua:
        { name = 'led', expr = '((GPIO_TypeDef *)0x50000000)->ODR', formula = 'bit(x, 5)' },  -- GPIOA on U0
        { name = 'led', expr = '*(unsigned int *)0x50000014',        formula = 'bit(x, 5)' },  -- raw GPIOA->ODR
  - With DEBUG = 0 there is no -g at all: nothing is readable, not even variables.
